# provenance: the one-shot consumption race family (the entity-domain
# DoubleTriggerRace scenarios, EntityEventBehaviorTests) — two guests trigger
# the SAME one-shot entity (MineExploded) in the same frame. The host executor
# consumes exactly once (the per-entity guard, the production TrapEffectApplier
# shape: EntityEventProfiles.IsOneShotConsumption + guard.Add); each guest's
# replay side executes exactly once (the relays cross, source-excluded: g1's
# trigger replays on g2, g2's on g1). A retransmission of an already-consumed
# trigger is relayed unconditionally (the message layer is not the guard — the
# guard lives on the consuming side) and dropped by both guards.
# Mechanism: TrapConsumptionRegistry.cs, EntityEventSync.cs (the executor's
# per-entity one-shot guard).
@0 event g1 MineExploded 10 20
@0 event g2 MineExploded 10 20
@33 expect executed MineExploded 1 within 500
@33 expect replayed g1 MineExploded 1 within 500
@33 expect replayed g2 MineExploded 1 within 500
@33 event g1 MineExploded 10 20
@66 expect executed MineExploded 1 within 500
@66 expect replayed g1 MineExploded 1 within 500
@66 expect replayed g2 MineExploded 1 within 500
